Portions of the browser goal loop are adapted from jev-ultrafast
(https://github.com/browser-use/jev-ultrafast), commit
1231850a0bf1a0c0341fe408ef1668dbbfdfac46, used under the MIT License.
`snapshot.js` is copied from `jev_ultrafast/snapshot.js` with the page global
renamed and the read installed once per document. The page driver
(`page.ts`), the loop, and the judge and text prompts are TypeScript ports of
`browser.py`, `agent.py`, `model.py`, and `questions.py`.

  Copyright (c) 2026 Browser Use

The Browser Harness daemon, screenshots, the demo, and the Python model
clients were dropped. The loop adds a risk screen, dialog and new-tab stops,
network-idle settling, and step and time budgets that are not in upstream.

